(version 1)
# The through-hole USB-C (GCT USB4085-GF-A, J1 / J4): GCT's recommended layout (drawing USB4085 rev B, sheet 2: 16 x
# 0.40 mm holes, 0.65 mm pads, 0.85 mm pitch) leaves 0.45 mm between neighbouring holes; JLC's general rule is 0.5 mm for
# different nets, but JLC stocks and wave-solders this part (C7095263) on this layout. Only between J1's / J4's own holes.
(rule "USB4085 holes per GCT's layout"
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && B.Type == 'Pad' && A.Parent == B.Parent && (A.Parent == 'J1' || A.Parent == 'J4')")
  (constraint hole_to_hole (min 0.44mm)))
